<DocsLayout title="Documentation">
  <h1>Hokkaido Language Documentation</h1>

  <p>
    Welcome to the Hokkaido language documentation. Hokkaido is a small, explicit,
    systems-programming language that compiles to native code via LLVM. It draws
    inspiration from Rust, C, and modern language design while keeping the feature
    set deliberately minimal.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting Started</h2>

  <p>
    Start with the <a href="/docs/syntax">Syntax Overview</a> for a high-level
    introduction to the language, then dive into specific topics:
  </p>

  <h2>Language Reference</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong><a href="/docs/syntax">Syntax Overview</a></strong> — Comments, basic structure, and a table of contents for the entire language.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href="/docs/syntax-types">Types & Variables</a></strong> — Primitive types, structs, enums, references, pointers, arrays, slices, tuples, function types, variables, scoping, and shadowing.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href="/docs/syntax-functions">Functions</a></strong> — Function declarations, parameters, return types, generics, turbofish, monomorphization, trait bounds, higher-order functions, and closures.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href="/docs/syntax-control-flow">Control Flow</a></strong> — If/else, for loops, break, continue, labeled break/continue, match, and region blocks.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href="/docs/syntax-expressions">Expressions</a></strong> — Operator precedence, comparison, logical, bitwise, arithmetic, shift, assignment, references and pointers, borrow checking, region blocks, raw pointers, atomics, constructors, function calls, and if-expressions.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href="/docs/syntax-data-structures">Data Structures</a></strong> — Arrays, structs (including generics), traits, impl blocks and method calls, enums, and their memory layout.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href="/docs/syntax-modules">Modules</a></strong> — Go-style packages, imports, visibility (pub), namespaces, and include.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href="/docs/syntax-ffi-cubical">C FFI & Cubical</a></strong> — C FFI declarations, variadic parameters, freestanding mode, inline assembly, and compile-time cubical evaluation.
    </li>
  </ul>

